IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `intl-nouns`

-- Antitrust Guidelines for International Enforcement and Cooperation (2017), chapter 2:
-- relevant antitrust and related statutes.
--
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW. Chapter 2 is "a brief summary of the antitrust and
-- related statutes" (2 [pdf page 7]); it is not the statutes, and every result here is the
-- 2017 text's account of one (the 2.7 and 2.8 names say so). Only the statements that are
-- tests the text itself states are encoded (fork F28): the preamble's two determinations (2),
-- the scope of the guidelines in the FTC Act (2.2), transactions outside the HSR Act (2.4),
-- the NCRPA's limit on damages for
-- notified ventures and its joint-production condition (2.7), the limits of the
-- Webb-Pomerene exemption (2.8), the export trade certificate of review (2.9), and the
-- limits of trade-dispute settlements and of officials' encouragement (2.12). The rest of
-- chapter 2, the statutes' prohibitions, penalties, waiting periods and dated figures, is
-- inert or out of scope (NOTES.md section 6). 2.6's one rule, that the IAEAA does not apply
-- to HSR materials, is encoded with 5.1.3 in intl-cooperation.l4, where the text repeats it.

§ `Chapter 2: relevant antitrust and related statutes`

§§ `2 The same substantive rules`

DECLARE `What chapter 2 says of the substantive rules` IS ONE OF
    `the agencies apply the same substantive rules to all cases, and do not discriminate based on the nationality of the parties`

-- 2 [pdf page 7]: "When the Agencies determine that a sufficient nexus to the United States
-- exists to apply the antitrust laws and that neither international comity nor the
-- involvement of a foreign jurisdiction precludes investigation or enforcement, the
-- Agencies apply the same substantive rules to all cases." Before both determinations the
-- sentence states nothing (NOTHING). The nationality of the parties is read by no rule.
@ref 2 [pdf page 7]; n.9, n.10 [pdf page 7]
GIVEN d IS A `Determinations before the same substantive rules apply (2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What chapter 2 says of the substantive rules`
`2: the substantive rules the agencies apply` MEANS
    IF     d's `the agencies determine that a sufficient nexus to the United States exists to apply the antitrust laws`
       AND d's `the agencies determine that neither international comity nor the involvement of a foreign jurisdiction precludes investigation or enforcement`
    THEN JUST `the agencies apply the same substantive rules to all cases, and do not discriminate based on the nationality of the parties`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `2.2 Federal Trade Commission Act`

-- 2.2 [pdf page 9]: "These International Guidelines pertain only to the Commission's
-- antitrust enforcement authority under Section 5's prohibition of unfair methods of
-- competition." "Only" closes the list, so the other prohibition is FALSE.
@ref 2.2 [pdf page 9]
GIVEN p IS A `Prohibition of Section 5 of the FTC Act (2.2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `2.2: the guidelines pertain to the Commission's authority under` p IF
    p EQUALS `the prohibition of unfair methods of competition`

§§ `2.4 Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act of 1976`

DECLARE `What section 2.4 says of a transaction` IS ONE OF
    `though the transaction is not subject to the HSR Act's notification and waiting period requirements, the agencies may seek to block or undo an anticompetitive merger or acquisition, or seek other equitable relief`

-- 2.4 [pdf page 11]: transactions not subject to the HSR Act's requirements "may still be
-- subject to the Sherman Act, the FTC Act, or the Clayton Act, and the Agencies may seek to
-- block or undo an anticompetitive merger or acquisition or seek other equitable relief when
-- any of those statutes applies." Whether a statute applies, and whether the merger is
-- anticompetitive, are findings. The sentence is about transactions not subject to the HSR
-- Act; for one that is, or when no statute applies, it states nothing (fork F25).
-- The waiting periods and the penalties of 2.4 are not encoded: the text says "The HSR Act
-- and the HSR Rules are necessarily technical and should be consulted directly" [pdf page
-- 12], and its figures are dated (n.32, n.38).
@ref 2.4 [pdf page 11]
GIVEN t IS A `Transaction and the HSR Act (2.4)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What section 2.4 says of a transaction`
`2.4: what the agencies may seek against a transaction` MEANS
    IF     (NOT t's `the transaction is subject to the HSR Act's notification and waiting period requirements`)
       AND t's `the Sherman Act, the FTC Act or the Clayton Act applies to the transaction`
    THEN JUST `though the transaction is not subject to the HSR Act's notification and waiting period requirements, the agencies may seek to block or undo an anticompetitive merger or acquisition, or seek other equitable relief`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `2.7 National Cooperative Research and Production Act`

DECLARE `What section 2.7 says of damages against a notified venture` IS ONE OF
    `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, monetary relief in a private civil suit is limited to actual, rather than treble, damages`
    `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the limit to actual damages applies only so long as the challenged conduct is within the scope of the notification`
    `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the benefit is not available to the joint production venture`

-- 2.7 [pdf pages 14-15]: "if participants provide notice to the Agencies, the amount of
-- monetary relief obtainable in a private civil suit ... is limited to actual, rather than
-- treble, damages so long as the challenged conduct is within the scope of the
-- notification. This benefit is not available to joint production ventures, unless" its two
-- conditions hold (the text quotes 15 U.S.C. 4306(2), n.52). Without notice the sentence
-- states nothing (NOTHING). Read in the text's order: notice, then scope, then the
-- joint-production condition (fork F20).
@ref 2.7 [pdf pages 14-15]; n.52 [pdf page 15]
GIVEN v IS A `Notified venture under the NCRPA (2.7)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What section 2.7 says of damages against a notified venture`
`2.7: damages against a notified venture` MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF NOT v's `the participants have provided notice to the agencies under the procedure`
      THEN NOTHING
      IF NOT v's `the challenged conduct is within the scope of the notification`
      THEN JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the limit to actual damages applies only so long as the challenged conduct is within the scope of the notification`
      IF     v's `the venture is a joint production venture`
         AND (NOT (    v's `the principal facilities for such production are located in the United States or its territories`
                   AND v's `each person who controls any party to the venture, the party included, is a United States person, or a foreign person from a country whose law accords antitrust treatment no less favorable to United States persons than to its domestic persons for participation in joint ventures for production`))
      THEN JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, the benefit is not available to the joint production venture`
      OTHERWISE JUST `as the 2017 text summarises the NCRPA, monetary relief in a private civil suit is limited to actual, rather than treble, damages`

§§ `2.8 Webb-Pomerene Act`

-- 2.8 [pdf page 15]: the limits of the exemption the text states, in its order.
DECLARE `Limit of the Webb-Pomerene exemption (2.8)` IS ONE OF
    `the exemption applies only to the export of goods, wares, or merchandise`
    `the exemption does not apply to conduct that has an anticompetitive effect in the United States`
    `the exemption does not apply to conduct that injures domestic competitors of the members of an export association`
    `associations seeking the exemption must file their articles of agreement and annual reports with the Commission`

@ref 2.8 [pdf page 15]
GIVEN a IS A `Export association (2.8)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Limit of the Webb-Pomerene exemption (2.8)`
`2.8: the limits of the exemption that the association meets` MEANS
    catMaybes (LIST (IF NOT a's `the exports are of goods, wares, or merchandise` THEN JUST `the exemption applies only to the export of goods, wares, or merchandise` ELSE NOTHING),
                    (IF a's `the conduct has an anticompetitive effect in the United States` THEN JUST `the exemption does not apply to conduct that has an anticompetitive effect in the United States` ELSE NOTHING),
                    (IF a's `the conduct injures domestic competitors of the members of the association` THEN JUST `the exemption does not apply to conduct that injures domestic competitors of the members of an export association` ELSE NOTHING),
                    (IF NOT a's `the association files its articles of agreement and annual reports with the Commission` THEN JUST `associations seeking the exemption must file their articles of agreement and annual reports with the Commission` ELSE NOTHING))

DECLARE `What section 2.8 says of the Webb-Pomerene exemption` IS ONE OF
    `within the limited antitrust exemption as the 2017 text describes it, which provides no immunity from prosecution under foreign antitrust laws`
    `outside the exemption, by a limit the 2017 text states`

-- 2.8 [pdf page 15]: "a limited antitrust exemption for the formation and operation of
-- associations of otherwise competing businesses to engage collectively in export sales."
-- An association that is not one is NOTHING. The first three limits are the text's own no
-- ("applies only", "does not apply"): meeting any is outside. The filing limit says "must
-- file" and states no consequence, so an association whose only limit is not filing is
-- NOTHING. One that meets none is within the exemption as the text describes it, which does
-- not "provide any immunity from prosecution under foreign antitrust laws". Pre-formation
-- approval is "not required", so no field asks for it (fork F21).
@ref 2.8 [pdf page 15]; n.53, n.54 [pdf page 15]
GIVEN a IS A `Export association (2.8)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What section 2.8 says of the Webb-Pomerene exemption`
`2.8: the Webb-Pomerene exemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF NOT a's `it is an association of otherwise competing businesses engaging collectively in export sales`
      THEN NOTHING
      IF null (`2.8: the limits of the exemption that the association meets` a)
      THEN JUST `within the limited antitrust exemption as the 2017 text describes it, which provides no immunity from prosecution under foreign antitrust laws`
      IF `2.8: the limits of the exemption that the association meets` a EQUALS LIST `associations seeking the exemption must file their articles of agreement and annual reports with the Commission`
      THEN NOTHING
      OTHERWISE JUST `outside the exemption, by a limit the 2017 text states`

§§ `2.9 Export Trading Company Act of 1982`

-- 2.9 [pdf page 16]: the four standards, in the text's order.
DECLARE `Standard for an export trade certificate of review (2.9)` IS ONE OF
    `neither a substantial lessening of competition or restraint of trade within the United States nor a substantial restraint of the export trade of any competitor of the applicant`
    `no unreasonable enhancement, stabilization, or depression of prices in the United States of the class of goods or services covered`
    `no unfair methods of competition against competitors engaged in the export of the class of goods or services exported by the applicant`
    `no act that may reasonably be expected to result in the sale for consumption or resale in the United States of such goods or services`

-- 2.9 [pdf page 16]: "To obtain an ETCR, an applicant must show that proposed export conduct
-- will" meet four standards. The standards not shown are listed; an empty list does not say
-- a certificate will issue (certificates "are issued by the Secretary of Commerce with the
-- concurrence of the Department").
@ref 2.9 [pdf page 16]; n.63 [pdf page 16]
GIVEN s IS A `Showing by an applicant for an export trade certificate of review (2.9)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Standard for an export trade certificate of review (2.9)`
`2.9: the standards the applicant has not shown` MEANS
    catMaybes (LIST (IF NOT s's `the applicant shows that the conduct will result in neither a substantial lessening of competition or restraint of trade within the United States nor a substantial restraint of the export trade of any competitor of the applicant` THEN JUST `neither a substantial lessening of competition or restraint of trade within the United States nor a substantial restraint of the export trade of any competitor of the applicant` ELSE NOTHING),
                    (IF NOT s's `the applicant shows that the conduct will not unreasonably enhance, stabilize, or depress prices in the United States of the class of goods or services covered by the application` THEN JUST `no unreasonable enhancement, stabilization, or depression of prices in the United States of the class of goods or services covered` ELSE NOTHING),
                    (IF NOT s's `the applicant shows that the conduct will not constitute unfair methods of competition against competitors engaged in the export of the class of goods or services exported by the applicant` THEN JUST `no unfair methods of competition against competitors engaged in the export of the class of goods or services exported by the applicant` ELSE NOTHING),
                    (IF NOT s's `the applicant shows that the conduct will not include any act that may reasonably be expected to result in the sale for consumption or resale in the United States of such goods or services` THEN JUST `no act that may reasonably be expected to result in the sale for consumption or resale in the United States of such goods or services` ELSE NOTHING))

DECLARE `What section 2.9 says of conduct under a certificate` IS ONE OF
    `the certificate is void from the outset, and offers no protection under the antitrust laws`
    `the conduct falls outside the scope of the certificate, and remains fully subject to private and governmental enforcement actions`
    `limited immunity from suit under both federal and state antitrust laws, within the limits section 2.9 states`

-- 2.9 [pdf pages 16-17]: persons named in the certificate "obtain limited immunity from suit
-- under both federal and state antitrust laws for activities that are specified in the
-- certificate and that comply with the terms of the certificate"; conduct "outside the scope
-- of a certificate remains fully subject to private and governmental enforcement actions";
-- a certificate "obtained by fraud is void from the outset". Fraud is read first, since a
-- void certificate has no scope; a person not named, or an activity not specified or not
-- complying, is read as outside its scope (fork F22).
@ref 2.9 [pdf pages 16-17]; n.62 [pdf page 16]
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under an export trade certificate of review (2.9)`
GIVETH A `What section 2.9 says of conduct under a certificate`
`2.9: conduct under a certificate` MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF c's `the certificate was obtained by fraud`
      THEN `the certificate is void from the outset, and offers no protection under the antitrust laws`
      IF     c's `the person is named in the certificate`
         AND c's `the activity is specified in the certificate`
         AND c's `the activity complies with the terms of the certificate`
      THEN `limited immunity from suit under both federal and state antitrust laws, within the limits section 2.9 states`
      OTHERWISE `the conduct falls outside the scope of the certificate, and remains fully subject to private and governmental enforcement actions`

-- 2.9 [pdf page 17]: the limits that remain on certified conduct, in the text's order.
DECLARE `Limit on certified conduct (2.9)` IS ONE OF
    `a person injured by certified conduct may recover actual, though not treble, damages if the conduct is found to violate any of the statutory criteria, and in such an action certified conduct enjoys a presumption of legality`
    `the certificate is no endorsement or opinion on the legality of the business plans under the laws of any foreign country`
    `the certificate does not insulate the conduct from investigation or enforcement by a foreign antitrust authority`
    `the Secretary of Commerce may revoke or modify the certificate`
    `the Department may bring suit under Section 15 of the Clayton Act to enjoin the conduct, even if it has been pre-approved as part of the certificate`

-- 2.9 [pdf page 17]: "The protections provided by an ETCR ... are not unlimited." The first
-- three limits hold of every certified activity; the Secretary's revocation needs the
-- determination of ceased compliance, and the Department's suit conduct that threatens "a
-- clear and irreparable harm to the national interest". For conduct with no immunity
-- (void, or outside the scope) the list is empty: section 2.9's other result says it all.
@ref 2.9 [pdf page 17]; n.65 to n.68 [pdf page 17]
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under an export trade certificate of review (2.9)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Limit on certified conduct (2.9)`
`2.9: the limits that remain on the certified conduct` MEANS
    IF `2.9: conduct under a certificate` c EQUALS `limited immunity from suit under both federal and state antitrust laws, within the limits section 2.9 states`
    THEN catMaybes (LIST (JUST `a person injured by certified conduct may recover actual, though not treble, damages if the conduct is found to violate any of the statutory criteria, and in such an action certified conduct enjoys a presumption of legality`),
                         (JUST `the certificate is no endorsement or opinion on the legality of the business plans under the laws of any foreign country`),
                         (JUST `the certificate does not insulate the conduct from investigation or enforcement by a foreign antitrust authority`),
                         (IF c's `the Secretary of Commerce or the Department determines that the export activities have ceased to comply with the statutory criteria` THEN JUST `the Secretary of Commerce may revoke or modify the certificate` ELSE NOTHING),
                         (IF c's `the conduct threatens a clear and irreparable harm to the national interest` THEN JUST `the Department may bring suit under Section 15 of the Clayton Act to enjoin the conduct, even if it has been pre-approved as part of the certificate` ELSE NOTHING))
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `2.12 Tariff Act of 1930`

DECLARE `What section 2.12 says of a trade-dispute settlement` IS ONE OF
    `the agreement is subject to the antitrust laws to the same extent as conduct unrelated to the settlement of a trade dispute`

-- 2.12 [pdf page 19]: "certain settlements of trade disputes entered under specific
-- procedures set forth in the U.S. trade laws are granted implied immunity under this Act,
-- even if the settlement involves price and quantity agreements". Agreements "that do not
-- comply with specific procedures in the U.S. trade laws or go beyond the measures authorized
-- by such laws, however, are subject to the antitrust laws to the same extent as conduct
-- unrelated to the settlement of a trade dispute." Only "certain" complying settlements are
-- immune and the text does not say which, so a complying settlement within the authorized
-- measures is NOTHING (fork F23). The price-and-quantity field is read by no rule.
@ref 2.12 [pdf page 19]; n.76 [pdf page 19]
GIVEN s IS A `Settlement of a trade dispute (2.12)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What section 2.12 says of a trade-dispute settlement`
`2.12: a trade-dispute settlement` MEANS
    IF    (NOT s's `the agreement complies with the specific procedures in the U.S. trade laws`)
       OR s's `the agreement goes beyond the measures authorized by such laws`
    THEN JUST `the agreement is subject to the antitrust laws to the same extent as conduct unrelated to the settlement of a trade dispute`
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What section 2.12 says of officials' involvement` IS ONE OF
    `the officials' involvement or encouragement, without more, does not immunize the arrangement`

-- 2.12 [pdf page 19]: "In the absence of legal authority, the fact, without more, that U.S.
-- or foreign government officials were involved in or encouraged measures that would
-- otherwise violate the antitrust laws does not immunize such arrangements." With legal
-- authority, or with no officials involved, the sentence states nothing.
@ref 2.12 [pdf page 19]; n.77 [pdf page 19]
GIVEN g IS A `Government officials and the measures (2.12)`
GIVETH A MAYBE `What section 2.12 says of officials' involvement`
`2.12: officials' involvement in the measures` MEANS
    IF     (NOT g's `there is legal authority for the measures`)
       AND g's `U.S. or foreign government officials were involved in or encouraged the measures`
    THEN JUST `the officials' involvement or encouragement, without more, does not immunize the arrangement`
    ELSE NOTHING
